 "answer": "In the LlamaIndex starter example, the save call is:\n\n```python\nindex.storage_context.persist()\n```\n\nIt writes to a directory named **`storage`** (`./storage`) by default. You can choose a different location with `persist_dir`, for example `index.storage_context.persist(persist_dir=\"./my_index\")`.\n\nTo reload it later, the starter pattern is `StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=\"./storage\")` followed by `load_index_from_storage(storage_context)`.\n\nI'm describing the starter tutorial as I know it. The exact API may have changed in newer LlamaIndex releases, so check the current docs if your code doesn't match.",
